.SH NAME
quanux-vault \- The Memory Vacuole (HDF5 Binary Journal)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B critique_vault.h5
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBquanux-vault\fR defines the structure of the Memory Vacuole. It is the repository where the cell records the exact sequence of its life cycle (every metabolic tick and execution).
.SH THE HDF5 SWMR DOCTRINE
The Vacuole uses \fBSWMR (Single Writer Multiple Reader)\fR capabilities within the HDF5 format. Like an RNA transcription process, the Vault listens to the Cytoplasm (\fBquanux-shm(4)\fR) and continuously appends raw 64-byte binary geometry exactly as it occurred physically on the CPU, without locking the execution loop.
.SH THE REPLICATION INTEGRITY PROOF
In order to prove to external entities (Auditors/Prop Firms) that the Simulated Cell mimics the Live Cell perfectly, the Vacuole maintains strict metadata:
.IP \[ci] 3
The SHA-256 Hash of the active Spreader Engine binary.
.IP \[ci] 3
The Databento Parquet Transpilation tables for offline 1:1 playback.

When an auditor inspects the Vacuole, they can forensically rebuild the exact cellular mitosis and state sequence, eliminating simulation drift.
